  "version": 2,
  "description": "Payment tokens a listing may show and a search may ask for (accepts). methods and wallets are how a person pays; agent are the ways an AI agent can pay at a door. labels name each token in English. synonyms read what a business says it accepts (schema.org paymentAccepted, a registration, a manifest), ignoring capitals and accents; marks read the payment providers seen in a site's own code, markup and files; handlers read the payment handlers a UCP profile names, word by word, the first whose words appear whole anywhere in the name; handlers_last, after them, the ones whose words must be the whole of the name's last part, after its last dot (dev.shopify.card is a card, pay_later_card is not). A brand's token is read only from words that name the brand. Anything else is left out. A token is never removed or renamed. Version 2 (18 Oct 2026): labels, handlers and handlers_last, bank_transfer apart from sepa, and afterpay, affirm, tabby, tamara, stripe_link, amazon_pay, visa_intelligent_commerce, mastercard_agent_pay, and ways people pay in every region: mpesa, interac, venmo, cash_app, zelle, bizum, paynow, promptpay, gcash, paypay, kakaopay, mercado_pago and oxxo.",
